    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1170">

                <pb facs="1182" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/121</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-29T12:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1916, 12 noon</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 30, 12.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3929. Your 3028, May 24, 6 p. m. Furnished copy of memorandum to the Minister of
                    Interior, Helfferich, to whom Chancellor referred me personally four days ago.
                    Talked over matter with Helfferich yesterday. Expect formal answer soon,
                    probably rejecting proposition. Have arranged conference to-day with
                    representatives of Foreign Office, Minister of the Interior, and requested the
                    disposition of representatives.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
